course: dictionary
lesson: 3510
title: Fate and the end of the story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Fate is one of these words. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «It is fate!» he said to himself. Here fate is a power that some people believe decides what will happen. The character feels that something was meant to happen, not that it was simply luck.
explain: «The fate of the ship» in a history book is different. It means what happened to the ship in the end, often something bad. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a belief in the future, or about how something ended? Then swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Fate is a noun: one fate, several fates.
fact: «Fate» means a power that some people believe decides what will happen in the future.
fact: «A person's fate» means what happens to them in the end, often something bad.
fact: «Tempt fate» means take a silly risk, as if you are daring bad luck to happen.
fact: «Seal someone's fate» means make the ending certain, often a bad one.
exercise: «Fate had other plans.» What does this mean? | Everyone agreed on the plan | Someone made a new plan for the picnic | Fate wrote the plans down in a book | *Something did not happen, or went wrong
exercise: «The fate of the ship» in a history book means what? | *What happened to the ship in the end | The name of the ship's captain | Where the ship was built | The fastest route across the sea
exercise: «It is fate!» he said to himself. What does fate suggest here? | A sore foot after the walk | *A belief that a power decided this would happen | A sandwich for lunch | A map of the seas
test: Mia says, «If you go out in that storm, you are tempting fate.» What does tempt fate mean? | Make a new friend | Take a silly risk | Sleep in late | *Take a silly risk, daring bad luck to happen | Hmm
test: «The vote seals his fate.» What does this suggest? | He will be given a medal | *The ending is now certain, often a bad one | The vote was postponed | He has forgotten the vote
exam: Ben reads, «Fate had other plans, so the match was cancelled.» Which word in the sentence helps you work out what fate means? | match | *plans | cancelled | so
